    {
        "text": "Xanthos remembers the day when he raised his oar at the Sargonian he had tied to the tree."
    },
    {
        "text": "But then he heard the horn of victory coming from the foothills, and the joyful Liberi brought news of the truce."
    },
    {
        "text": "The frightened Sargonian stumbled and fell as he fled. Xanthos's comrades held him back and prevented him from killing the prisoner."
    },
    {
        "text": "Slowly but surely, resentment began to build within his heart."
    },
    {
        "text": "Life and vitality were gone from the soil of his homeland, but the marks that the Sargonians left behind linger."
    },
    {
        "text": "Their banners, their landmines. The dam they built, which killed the river, became an indelible scar upon the land."
    },
    {
        "text": "He saw many Sargonians make a hurried retreat towards the border on his way to Athenius."
    },
    {
        "text": "He never joined the Minoans who threw rocks and spat at them, because it was not enough."
    },
    {
        "text": "In Athenius, he rowed his ferry on the Delphi Canal day after day. He watched over the ebb and flow of the canal, but he could not keep the river of his own heart in check."
    },
    {
        "text": "Rage roiled in his heart, seeking an opening."
    },
    {
        "command": "dialog"
    },
    {
        "command": "blocker",
        "params": {
